  "starterCode": "import numpy as np\n\ndef dl_vanilla_rnn_cell(x_seq: list, h_0: list, W_xh: list, W_hh: list, b_h: list) -> dict:\n    pass",
  "solution": "### 💡 Intuition & Approach\nThe implementation computes **Vanilla RNN Cell** by following direct mathematical principles, leveraging vectorized operations to ensure both correctness and optimal runtime efficiency.\n\n### ⚡ Python Reference Implementation\n```python\nimport numpy as np\n\ndef dl_vanilla_rnn_cell(x_seq: list, h_0: list, W_xh: list, W_hh: list, b_h: list) -> dict:\n    X, h = np.array(x_seq, dtype=np.float64), np.array(h_0, dtype=np.float64)\n    Wxh, Whh, bh = np.array(W_xh, dtype=np.float64), np.array(W_hh, dtype=np.float64), np.array(b_h, dtype=np.float64)\n    all_h = []\n    for xt in X:\n        h = np.tanh(np.dot(Wxh, xt) + np.dot(Whh, h) + bh)\n        all_h.append(np.round(h, 4).tolist())\n    return {'final_hidden': np.round(h, 4).tolist(), 'all_hidden_states': all_h}\n```\n\n### ⏱️ Complexity Analysis\n- **Time Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ where $N$ represents the size of the primary input.\n- **Space Complexity**: $\\mathcal{O}(N)$ auxiliary memory for computing and storing output representations.",
